The initial identification path was based on the file 5.48 behavior in
src/apprentice.c (compiled database layout), src/softmagic.c (pattern
matching, name/use, descriptions), src/ascmagic.c and src/encoding.c
(text fallback), and src/fsmagic.c (empty and unreadable files).
It does not link libmagic and contains no cgo.

The scanner compatibility target is FILE5_41 (file/libmagic 5.41), not
FILE5_48. fsmagic.go now follows FILE5_41 src/fsmagic.c and src/magic.c
for the scanner's MAGIC_NONE and MAGIC_MIME_TYPE|MAGIC_SYMLINK|MAGIC_ERROR
handles. Its upstream copyright and license are retained in that file.
encoding.go and ascmagic.go follow FILE5_41 src/encoding.c and
src/ascmagic.c, including the 65536-byte encoding limit, UTF-16 code-unit
behavior and incomplete UTF-8 handling. Both retain the upstream license.
json.go and csv.go follow FILE5_41 src/is_json.c and src/is_csv.c,
respectively, and retain their upstream licenses. These are format
detectors with 5.41's permissive behavior, not general data validators.
cdf.go and cdf_summary.go follow FILE5_41 src/cdf.c, src/readcdf.c and
src/cdf_time.c for the scanner's two handles, retaining their upstream
licenses. They read allocation chains, directory records and summary
properties; no document type or Windows version is inferred from a raw
byte substring. File reads use the same open descriptor beyond the
initial prefix, whereas Buffer has no out-of-buffer source.
elf.go, elf_notes.go and elf_core.go follow the complete runtime paths in
FILE5_41 src/readelf.c and src/elfclass.h, retaining the upstream licenses.
ELF analysis supplies a suffix and mode flags before softmagic; the loaded
database, not a parallel Go architecture table, supplies the base type and
MIME. Buffer intentionally does not run fd-based ELF analysis.
MIME annotations follow FILE5_41 softmagic.c handle_annotation/varexpand,
with a 1024-byte expansion buffer. An annotation ends its current match,
not every caller: after use/indirect returns, a caller can append its own
or a later annotation, or fail after the nested MIME was printed.
An empty Buffer uses application/x-empty from funcs.c file_default;
an empty regular File is handled earlier by fsmagic as inode/x-empty.
String, Pascal string and search extents follow FILE5_41 softmagic.c
mget: an empty match at EOF is allowed, but a start beyond EOF is not.
